{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# End-to-End Distributed Training Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `MiniGPT`: 2-layer transformer with masked self-attention and a separate LM head."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `make_corpus(seed, total_tokens)`: deterministic next-token-prediction data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `_train_worker`: spawned per rank; broadcasts init params, runs the loop, calls ZeRO step, writes the sharded checkpoint at step 10."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `verify_resume`: after the main run, reloads the step-10 checkpoint in-process and asserts the saved master shards match the in-memory snapshot byte-for-byte."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `main`: orchestrates the whole demo, prints the loss table, the memory profile, and the verification result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: a 20-row loss table, a 4-row per-rank memory profile, a checkpoint manifest, and a \"RESUME VERIFIED\" line on success."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a tensor-parallel split of the attention head and verify the loss matches the single-rank baseline. Two ranks: half the heads per rank, allreduce of the attention output.\n2. Add gradient accumulation across 4 microbatches and prove the gradient equals the gradient of one big batch.\n3. Add a resume-from-step-10 path that actually continues training to step 20 and produces the same final loss as the original run.\n4. Add a metrics export (loss, grad norm, step time) to JSONL so the run can be visualised after the fact.\n5. Add a NaN guard that rolls back to the previous checkpoint on a loss spike, and force a spike with a one-step LR multiplier to exercise the rollback."
      ]
    }
  ],
